From 378ddb52617f6cc4bec43e62d1a06654fd62e6a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 22:39:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rs: zero-on-clear ROOT FIX - cross-request recurrent-state
 leak was the residual F-136 mechanism

Minimal repro (ring_content_probe.py repeat mode): same request 3x on one server with ring
planes allocated (FORCE_RS_SEQ=5, NO drafter, NO rollback) returned 3 DIFFERENT outputs on
Vulkan, two echoing the prompt - the next sequence started from the previous request's
recurrent state (the original 'seeded at prefill' signature). The in-graph rs_z zeroing does
not reliably clear state on Vulkan when the bank planes exist. Fix: on rm_all seq_rm with
n_rs_seq>0, hard-zero the cell's rows across every plane host-side (backend-independent;
LLAMA_RS_NO_ZERO_ON_CLEAR opt-out).

Validated:
- repeat repro: 3/3 byte-identical after fix (was 0/3)
- rollback probe (cache-trim rollbacks, 4B): Vulkan ring-vs-fresh 3/4 (was 0/4; CPU 3/4)
- 27B Huihui + DFlash2 ring: depth 3 = 8.74 t/s, depth 5 = 6.02, depth 7 = 5.30,
  ZERO degenerate at every depth (depth 5/7 previously looped hard). Diffs vs plain remain
  the graph-layout tie-flip class, eyeballed fluent.

Also rides: RESTORE-HASH + CLEAR-HASH trace probes (LLAMA_RS_TRACE), rs_pending age-relabel
experiment behind LLAMA_RS_AGE_FIX (default OFF - measured no better), rs_shift in
llm_graph_input_rs::can_reuse, huge-row GET_ROWS cases in test-backend-ops.
